  "literal_target": "g_{\\eta}(y)=\\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})+\\eta^{-1/2}\\,\\mathbb{E}_{\\mathsf{r}_{y}}\\nabla\\rho_{y}(U)\\,,\\qquad\\widehat{g}_{\\eta}(y;G)=\\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})+\\eta^{-1/2}\\,\\nabla\\rho_{y}(G)\\,.",
  "literal_definitions": {
    "S1.E1": "\\alpha I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V(x)\\preceq\\beta I\\,,\\qquad x\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}\\,,\\qquad\\kappa\\coloneqq\\frac{\\beta}{\\alpha}\\,. (1.1)",
    "S2.p1.1": "Except in the generic warm start result Theorem 6.1 and its consequence Theorem 7.1 , throughout the remainder of the paper V\\in C^{2}(\\mathbb{R}^{d}) and ( 1.1 ) holds pointwise. For most of the paper, we normalize \\beta=1 , so that \\kappa^{-1}I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V\\preceq I ; this can be achieved by rescaling.",
    "S2.E1": "\\operatorname{prox}_{aV}(y)\\coloneqq\\operatorname*{argmin}_{x\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}}{\\Bigl\\{V(x)+\\frac{\\lVert x-y\\rVert^{2}}{2a}\\Bigr\\}}\\,. (2.1)",
    "S2.Ex1": "R_{a,y}(\\mathrm{d}x)\\propto\\exp\\Bigl\\{-V(x)-\\frac{\\lVert x-y\\rVert^{2}}{2a}\\Bigr\\}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,.",
    "S3.SS1.p1.1": "For a smoothing variance \\eta>0 , write",
    "S3.SS1.p2.1": "The smoothed potential V_{\\eta} , defined by e^{-V_{\\eta}}\\coloneqq e^{-V}*\\mathsf{N}(0,\\eta I) , is given by",
    "S3.E1": "\\nabla V_{\\eta}(y)=\\mathbb{E}\\bigl[\\nabla V(X)\\bigm|X+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,G=y\\bigr]\\,, (3.1)",
    "S3.SS1.p3.2": "The intuition is that \\nabla V_{\\eta}(y)=\\int\\nabla V\\,\\mathrm{d}R_{\\eta,y} , and \\law(\\operatorname{prox}_{\\eta V}(y)+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,G)\\approx R_{\\eta,y} , so that \\widehat{g}_{\\eta}(y;G) is almost an unbiased estimator of \\nabla V_{\\eta}(y) .",
    "S4.Ex3": "x_{y}^{+}\\coloneqq\\operatorname{prox}_{\\eta V}(y)\\,.",
    "S4.Ex8": "\\rho_{y}(u)\\coloneqq V(x_{y}^{+}+\\sqrt{\\eta}u)-V(x_{y}^{+})-\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,\\langle\\nabla V(x_{y}^{+}),u\\rangle\\,.",
    "S4.SS1.p4.1": "Proximal optimality gives \\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})=(y-x_{y}^{+})/\\eta . Define",
    "S4.SS1.p4.2": "Then 0\\preceq\\nabla^{2}\\rho_{y}\\preceq\\eta I , and under R_{\\eta,y} , (X-x_{y}^{+})/\\sqrt{\\eta} has density proportional to u\\mapsto e^{-\\lVert u\\rVert^{2}/2-\\rho_{y}(u)} . Call this law \\mathsf{r}_{y} . We have"
